VIEWS
********************************************************************************************
A View is a virtual table created from the result of a SQL query. It stores the query definition and presents data from one or more underlying tables.

Command : check all view in our databases 

SHOW FULL TABLES WHERE table_type = 'VIEW';

-> SHOW FULL TABLES;  [Check views exits]

-> SELECT DATABASES (); [check current databases]
  
Practice :

---> Check your table:
  
  SELECT * FROM students;

---> Create a view:

  CREATE VIEW student_view AS SELECT id, name FROM students;

---> Display the view :

  SELECT * FROM students_view;


