***********************************************************************************************************
AGGREGATE FUNCTION
***************************************************************************************************
1.COUNT() : COUNT() is an aggregate function used to count the number of rows in a table.

  Command : SELECT COUNT(*) FROM table_name;

  Example : SELECT COUNT(*) FROM customers;

2.SUM() : SUM() is an aggregate function used to calculate the total of all numeric values in a column.

  Command : SELECT SUM(column_name) FROM table_name;

  Example : SELECT SUM(price) FROM products;


3.AVG() : AVG() is an aggregate function used to calculate the average value of a numeric column.


  Command : SELECT AVG(column_name) FROM table_name;

  Example : SELECT AVG(price) FROM products;


4.MAX() : MAX() is an aggregate function used to find the highest value in a column.

  Command : SELECT MAX(column_name) FROM table_name;

  Example : SELECT MAX(price) FROM products;

5.MIN() : MIN() is an aggregate function used to find the lowest value in a column.

  Command : SELECT MIN(column_name) FROM table_name;

  Example : SELECT MIN(price) FROM products;

