*****************************************************************************************************
An Index is a database object that helps MySQL find rows faster when searching or retrieving data from a table

Syntax : CREATE INDEX index_name 
         ON table_name(column_name);

B-TREE = Balenced TREE is the index structure MySQL commonly uses to organize indexed values so that it can search, sort, and find ranges efficiently.


Example : CREATE INDEX idx_employee_name
          ON employees(emp_name);

VERIFY : SHOW INDEX FROM employees;

DROP INDEX FROM TABLE : 

 command & Example : DROP INDEX idx_employee_name ON employees;
