1. UNIQUE INDEX : A UNIQUE INDEX is an index that prevents duplicate values in a column while also providing an index for that column.

Syntax : CREATE UNIQUE INDEX index_name
         ON table_name(column_name);

Example : CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_unique_email
          ON employee_details(email); 

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX → Create
SHOW INDEX          → View
EXPLAIN             → Check usage
DROP INDEX          → Remove

EXAPLIN  : to diagnose, profile, and optimize database queries by forcing the database optimizer to reveal its execution plan
===================================================================================================
2. COMPOSITE INDEX : A Composite index is an index created one or more columns of a table

Syntax : CREATE INDEX idx_name
         ON table_name(column 1, column 2);

column1 -> First indexed column

column2 -> Second indexed column 

Example : CREATE INDEX idx_name_manager
          ON employees(emp_name, manager_id);

