* GROUP BY CLAUSE: GROUP BY is a sql clause used to group of rows that have same values in one or more columns usally to perform the aggregate functions such as COUNT(), AVG(), MIN(), SUM(), and MAX().

Syntax : SELECT column_name , Aggregate_function(column_name)
         FROM table_name
         GROUP BY column_name;

Example: SELECT customer_id, COUNT(*)
         FROM orders
         GROUP BY customer_id;



